  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Leidos reports $2.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, with 3,035 awards and an average award size of $745K. Obligations fell 25.6% year over year. The Department of Defense is the single largest buyer, obligating $1.6B so far in FY2026 to date. Other significant buying agencies include the Department of Homeland Security with $392M and the Department of Transportation with $146M. Computer Systems Design Services and Computer Facilities Management Services are the top NAICS markets for FY2026 to date, with $652M and $590M respectively. Electronic Computer Manufacturing, Engineering Services, and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance follow, with $310M, $230M, and $227M respectively. Fiscal-year history shows obligations rising from $1.9B in FY21 to peaks of $3B in FY24 and FY25, then registering $2.3B in FY26 to date. The figures shown are contract obligations except where tables note award-value as total contract values. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Leidos's biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the largest customer with $1.6B in FY2026 to date. Department of Homeland Security follows with $392M, and Department of Transportation follows with $146M. General Services Administration and Department of Health and Human Services recorded $79.5M and $50.6M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What federal markets drive Leidos's revenue?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services and Computer Facilities Management Services are the top markets with $652M and $590M in FY2026 to date. Electronic Computer Manufacturing, Engineering Services, and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance contribute $310M, $230M, and $227M respectively. Other listed markets include Computing Infrastructure Providers at $146M and research categories at $14.3M and $13.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
