      "q": "How much does Leidos make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Leidos earns $2.3B in federal contract obligations FY2026 to date. Leidos received 3,035 awards with an average award size of $745K, and obligations fell 25.6% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Leidos?",
      "a": "Department of Defense is the largest agency buyer, obligating $1.6B in FY2026 to date. Other buying agencies include Department of Homeland Security ($392M), Department of Transportation ($146M), General Services Administration ($79.5M), Department of Health and Human Services ($50.6M), and Department of the Interior ($6.7M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Leidos sell to the government?",
      "a": "Leidos sells IT and engineering services and related products to the federal government. Top markets for FY2026 to date include Computer Systems Design Services ($652M), Computer Facilities Management Services ($590M), Electronic Computer Manufacturing ($310M), Engineering Services ($230M), and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance ($227M)."
